Testing logical operators:
  c = been, d = run
  AND (c && d): been
  OR (c || d): run
  NOT (!c): run
  NOT (!d): been
  Compound AND (c && !d): been
  Compound OR (!c || d): run
  Complex expression (c && (d || !d)): been
  Complex expression ((c || d) && (c || !d)): been
\nLogical operations with integers:
  x = 10, y = 20
  Comparison in logical expression ((x > 5) && (y < 30)): run
  Comparison in logical expression ((x > 15) || (y < 30)): run
\nLogical operations with decimals:
  a = 10.5, b = 20.25
  Comparison in logical expression ((a > 5.5) && (b < 30.5)): run
  Comparison in logical expression ((a > 15.5) || (b < 30.5)): run
\nLogical operations with mixed types:
  Integer vs. Decimal ((x < a) && (y > b)): been
  Integer vs. Decimal ((x > a) || (y > b)): been
\nAssignment of logical operation (result = (x < y) && (c || d)): run
